# Phase 18 P18-V01 `MqClientAdmin.deleteTopicInBroker` — 2026-10-18T03:12:12Z

## Scope and source

- Continued on `phase/19-phase-18-compatibility-release-gate`; the pinned Java
  oracle at `/Users/bruce.tsai/Projects/3rd/rocketmq` remained read-only.
- Reconciled Java 5.5.1 `MqClientAdminImpl.deleteTopicInBroker`: request code
  215, direct Broker address, `DeleteTopicRequestHeader`, no body, null result
  on `SUCCESS`, and `MQClientException` with response code/remark otherwise.
- Java's header has a nullable annotated topic because `checkFields()` is a
  no-op. It inherits nullable `ns`, `nsd`, `bname`, `oway`, and `lo`; inherited
  equality/hash only considers the four RPC base fields.

## Implementation

- Added the public Rust header, RPC-base equality semantics, validation and
  typed-header inventory/cross-decode coverage, and
  `MQClientApi::delete_topic_in_broker`.
- Extended the invoked Java `MqClientAdmin` fixture with success and Broker
  error cases; added scripted Core tests that compare request code/fields and
  Broker error mapping. Updated the Phase 17 matrix to 7/19 after the code
  commit `74c52143` (`feat(admin): add delete topic in broker RPC`).
- The first attempt to invoke the Java fixture generator supplied a fixture
  path to the fixed `compat.Main` entry point and returned its usage text. The
  existing `request-header-identity-fixture` and
  `mq-client-admin-fixtures` dispatchers were then used successfully.
- Preserved the pre-existing uncommitted Phase 19 README, differential runner,
  local runner, and its execution log; none were included in this slice.

